      "failure": "Both active modules retain a module-global _preflight_gate(operation) ordinary callable. It accepts an arbitrary caller callback, passes that callback the lexical raw load_external function and the loaded v9 harness ModuleType, and returns the callback result without constraining its type. An unchanged-byte caller therefore obtains and retains both the raw loader and harness. The escaped loader accepts an arbitrary Path and module name and can load the declared subject-driver module without an execution root or the runtime freeze/dependency plus static route/schedule/nonce sequence. The returned harness also constructs and returns the 97-cell semantic module. This contradicts the candidate claims that no raw semantic loader or authority object is returned and that preflight cannot authorize runtime work. The stored static checker inspects callback parameters only on _root_bound_operation, then declares authority_objects_publicly_returned=0 without checking _preflight_gate's callback parameter or return expression.",
